ions), requires deep expertise in RF theory, antenna design, and space industry standards (NR NTN, DVB-S2x, ECSS), which are entirely absent from the candidate's profile. \\n\\n**Critical Technical Gaps:**\\n1.  **Domain Mismatch:** The candidate's expertise is in Cloud, AI, and Web Development (Python, Java, React, RAG, LLMs). The JD requires expertise in RF systems, satellite communications, and space payloads. There is zero overlap in core technical domains.\\n2.  **Educational Discrepancy:** The JD requires an M.S. in Electrical, Aerospace, or Systems Engineering. The candidate holds a B.S. in Computer Science and a M.S. in Applied Data Science/AI. While related fields, the fundamental physics and engineering principles of RF and Space systems are missing.\\n3.  **Experience Deficit:** The JD mandates 5+ years of systems engineering in space/defense platforms. The candidate has only 1.5 years of experience, primarily in AI/Software projects.\\n4.  **Toolchain Absence:** The role demands proficiency in DOORS (requirements), MATLAB/Simulink (modeling), and Vector CANoe (vehicle network testing). The candidate's toolset consists of Python libraries, RAG pipelines, and cloud infrastructure, with no mention of automotive/space engineering tools.\\n5.  **Standards Compliance:** The JD requires knowledge of ISO 26262 (Automotive Safety) and Space standards (ECSS). The candidate has no documented experience with safety-critical development or formal standards compliance.\\n\\n**Conclusion:**\\nThis is a fundamental mismatch. The candidate is a Software/Data Engineer, while the role is a Systems Engineer with a focus on RF/Space hardware and standards. The candidate's skills in AI and Cloud are irrelevant to the core requirements of designing satellite communication payloads, defining RF interfaces, or leading system-level trade studies in the automotive/space sector. The compatibility score of 5% reflects the minimal overlap in general engineering soft skills (e.g., documentation, system design concepts) but acknowledges the complete lack of technical alignment with the must-have requirements. Hiring this candidate would require an extensive, likely prohibitive, retraining period to bridge the gap from AI/Software engineering to RF/Space Systems Engineering.\"}"
